From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: include serialized priority in bounded range trace

Use the existing shared 32-row range trace budget. Only two numeric header
fields are retained; no payload, identifier or network data is logged. This
allows the real-device round to check the command field after serialization,
without assuming the host-only header block test proves firmware scheduling.

---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
@@ -2688,6 +2688,11 @@
 
 	ath12k_wmi_copy_scan_event_cntrl_flags(cmd, arg);
 
+	if (ar->scan.range_req &&
+	    atomic_inc_return(&ar->scan.range_trace_count) <= 32)
+		ath12k_info(ar->ab, "phone range header priority=%u state11d=%u\n",
+			    le32_to_cpu(cmd->scan_priority), ar->state_11d);
+
 	cmd->dwell_time_active = cpu_to_le32(arg->dwell_time_active);
 	cmd->dwell_time_active_2g = cpu_to_le32(arg->dwell_time_active_2g);
 	cmd->dwell_time_passive = cpu_to_le32(arg->dwell_time_passive);
